    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“So your coworkers finally got to you, huh?” I gesture to the boxes, forcing myself to focus on what’s in front of me no",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2344
        },
        {
          "text": "Jess sighs. “I told them I didn’t want a shower. They wouldn’t take no for an answer.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2498
        },
        {
          "text": "“As long as I have the wedding dress I want, and you’re there, nothing else matters.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2773
        }
      ],
      "words": 65
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Jess is already laughing. “Jesus, I forgot about this one.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3622
        },
        {
          "text": "We’re sitting cross-legged on the floor of my sister’s spare bedroom, the box of childhood pictures our mom didn’t take ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3680
        },
        {
          "text": "A young, gap-toothed Lucy grins back at me. “School picture.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3951
        },
        {
          "text": "Jess’s smile right now is at least as wide as mine is in the photo, though hers has several more teeth",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4011
        }
      ],
      "words": 72
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“Just because you haven’t had a job yet that values you for who you are doesn’t mean you don’t have skills,” Jess says",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5770
        },
        {
          "text": "“You have a huge heart. You’re fiercely loyal. If you make a mistake—”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5921
        },
        {
          "text": "“You also protect the people you care about. Look at this.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6113
        },
        {
          "text": "In this picture I have a huge black garbage bag in my hands, stuffed full of trash",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6667
        }
      ],
      "words": 67
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "In this moment I make up my mind",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7880
        },
        {
          "text": "I will either convince the Agency to give me my life back—or die trying",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7914
        },
        {
          "text": "With these I can paint a real picture of Lucy McKenzie. What she’s done. What she’s learned. And all the terribly human ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8152
        }
      ],
      "words": 49
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Daniel is waiting for me on the couch when I get back from Jess’s house armed with a ton of old pictures",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7987
        },
        {
          "text": "“Images from a life well lived,” he murmurs",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9054
        },
        {
          "text": "I’m not so sure about that. “A life lived, anyway.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9097
        },
        {
          "text": "“I know the current Lucy pretty well, I think.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9558
        },
        {
          "text": "“I want to know every version of you.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9834
        }
      ],
      "words": 61
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "It will end, though. And soon. If tonight is one of the last times I’ll get to experience this kind of intimacy, I want ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10699
        },
        {
          "text": "“For so long, I existed only for my responsibilities,” he tells me, so gently",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 14039
        },
        {
          "text": "“They mean nothing to me anymore. Now, there is only you.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 14143
        }
      ],
      "words": 60
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“We should leave soon,” he says, apologetic. “It’s Monday morning, which is always a busy time. We’ll be more likely to ",
          "ok": true,
